{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you shall tell your son.</b> Who does not know how to ask — you shall say to him thus: what did HaKadosh Baruch Hu see to give the Egyptians strength to drive us out of their land before our fathers' dough had time to become leavened? Does He not have it in His power to keep us there until it leavens, and until they prepare provisions for the way? The answer to this: <b>because of this</b> — that I have taken upon myself to fulfill the commandments of pesaḥ, maẓẓah, and maror — <b>HaShem did for me</b> the miracles when I went out of Egypt." "<b>Because of this HaShem did for me.</b> Rashi's commentary hints at an answer to the wicked son — namely, this thing you shall tell to the son who does not know how to ask. And from the word <b>לי</b> we learn that this too is an answer to the wicked son — namely, 'for me' and not for you."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "The text attributes to Rashi an answer to the wicked son, though the verse context is the son who does not know how to ask; this is rendered as the compiler wrote it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:39.444059256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}